WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.540
When I first started,

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.650
I got a phone call from a woman

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.740
whose daughter was an equestrian

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.960
and the woman was very upset

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.720
because her daughter's
coach had been removed,

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.010
had been banned by the
Center for SafeSport

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.730
for sexual misconduct.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.480
I was assuming that she was calling to

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.840
kind of talk through
what that really meant.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.170
Instead, she called me
to ask me to remove him

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.820
from our disciplinary database,

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.570
even though he had been removed with cause

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.380
because it was her daughter's coach,

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.130
and that was the only coach that

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.420
her daughter would work with.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.180
And I just found it, just mind blowing

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.270
that here you have a mother,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.300
who I'm sure loves her daughter very much

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.310
and wants nothing but
the best for her child.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:52.440
But at the same time was
willing to put her child at risk

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.510
with someone who shouldn't
have been around kids.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.730
Who had done some pretty terrible things

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.923
because she wanted her child to win.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.510
What I didn't realize

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.710
when I first began reporting this story,

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:09.220
is how deep the divisions
run with an equestrian.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.148
This is a community that has
been torn apart by SafeSport.

00:01:13.148 --> 00:01:14.680
SafeSport is an agency

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.940
that was established by Congress in 2017,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.770
to effectively be the watchdog

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.110
over all Olympic sporting communities,

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.630
when it comes to sexual misconduct.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.330
The center has been criticized
by a number of Olympic sports

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:31.230
for not doing enough to support survivors.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.420
But what surprised me

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.240
about the equestrian
community in particular,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.560
is that here we are seeing members

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.010
actually push back against SafeSport

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.520
in defense of the accused.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.480
I was kind of like

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.960
SafeSport is this third party organization

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.770
but they need to like mind
their own business in a way

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.480
and stay out of the USEF.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.200
Not only are they challenging
the center's process,

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.800
but they are demanding
for the reinstatement

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.360
of some athletes who have been
brought down by the center.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.160
This was the first time that these people

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.430
were are being held accountable

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:06.910
and accountability makes
people uncomfortable.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.210
Equestrian, like many sports,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.640
is having to kind of have a reckoning

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.150
within their community.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.300
And some are not happy about it.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.350
These families are wealthy.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.400
We're talking about the
daughters of billionaires,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.080
of rock stars, of royalty.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.360
This is a community that is not afraid

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.440
to stand up for what it believes in,

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.190
to challenge or to question authorities.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.690
And it's definitely
not afraid to push back

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.940
when it thinks they're getting it wrong.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.270
People can mobilize to make change.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.360
That's how the Center for
SafeSports started, right?

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.020
People were angry, they wanted change

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.110
and they saw change happen.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.400
So I've got no issue with that

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.756
but you gotta ask yourself,

00:02:44.756 --> 00:02:48.190
why are you vocal against an organization

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.940
that is holding people accountable?

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:09.780
When I was nine years old,
eight or nine years old,

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:12.650
I went to Sacramento International

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.430
and it was a World Cup
qualifiers was a big 160 class.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.010
And I remember just watching that class

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.810
thinking that's gonna be me one day.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.290
I had no doubt in my mind

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.190
that that's what I was gonna be doing.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.970
Two years later, same show,

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:30.790
I was sitting in those same stands.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:35.430
I was watching the World's
Cup qualifier and Rich won it.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.460
And I remember being so
amazed by Rich and Flexible,

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:39.660
and I thought, okay, that's
who I need to ride with

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.910
to get to the top of the sport.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.680
Rich Fellers is an Olympic team veteran.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.680
He won the 2012 World Cup
Final in the Netherlands.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.100
He was probably one of the most respected

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.480
and well known trainers in the country.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.258
Rich Fellers and Flexible, 26.61 to beat

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:04.020
and he did it, what a tremendous.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.050
I talked to many young women

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:10.660
who at the age of 14 or
15 moved across cities

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.030
in order to be able to ride

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.280
at an elite level with a top trainer,

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.140
some who even moved to different countries

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.300
because they knew that was the trainer

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.890
that was gonna get them on the path

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.470
of where they wanted to go,

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.543
where they felt like they needed to go.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:30.900
When I was 14, is when I
decided to move to the Fellers.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.930
They were in Oregon and
I was in California.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:37.000
And so it was kind of
agreed upon by everyone

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.033
that I would go and stay with them.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.670
Maggie from the day she was born

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.610
was always very independent.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.650
She would never even hold
my hand when she was two.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:49.900
She just was so intense and
so focused and so driven.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:52.910
So when she decided she
wanted to go up to Oregon

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.217
and ride with the Fellers we said,

00:04:54.217 --> 00:04:56.417
'Okay, we can make that happen.'

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:04.170
Maggie's routine was so
straightforward and so strong.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.350
She would get up at 7:00 AM.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.183
She would get ready.

00:05:06.183 --> 00:05:07.600
She would drive to the barn.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.090
If she wasn't riding at the barn

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.820
she was working at the barn.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.430
And then she would go home,

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:14.790
take a shower, do some
schoolwork, go to sleep

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.940
and get up the next
day and go to the barn.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.960
Your relationship with your trainer

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.993
is probably strongest
relationship in your life.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:29.130
They build you up and they
teach you everything you know

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.603
and you grow as a person when
you're training with them.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:37.290
The more time you spend with
them, the more you trust them.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:41.023
And they are the strongest
voice in your life.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:46.560
I think that that
relationship is important.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:49.680
But I think in my case,
the line is crossed.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.550
And I think in a lot of
cases, the line gets crossed

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:57.320
Maggie Kehring under the
watchful eye of Rich Fellers.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:00.810
We had just had a Christmas party.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.610
It was like a big barn Christmas party.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.100
The Fellers' invited all their friends

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.580
and nothing happened there.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:10.800
It was two days after I got this call

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.110
and he was like,

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:14.070
'something's just been
building up inside me

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.850
the past six months.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.270
I'm crazy about you.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.360
I have these really
strong feelings about you.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.780
You can't tell anyone,
this is very personal'

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.340
but he's like, 'it's okay, don't worry.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.670
I'll get it under control
and everything will be fine.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.170
I'll go back to normal.'

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.120
And I remember just sitting in shock.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.260
How old were you?

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.383
I was 16.

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:45.570
The moment the announcement was made

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.800
that I was gonna be the CEO,

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.750
I remember later that day

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:53.810
getting a direct message
on Facebook of all places

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:57.070
from this woman who
happened to be an equestrian

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:00.230
basically warning me of
what I was stepping into

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.640
and that I really needed
to take a close look

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:06.570
at the entire community at
the Center for SafeSport,

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:10.143
because it was going to be tough for me.

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:13.490
Mom,

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.150
don't you wanna know why coach
keeps texting me so much.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.810
The U.S. Center for SafeSport

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:21.320
is a nonprofit 501c3 organization

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.870
that opened its doors back in 2017

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.520
which is right in the middle of the midst

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:29.670
of the Larry Nassar scandal
with USA gymnastics.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.270
This morning, dozens of
Larry Nassar's victims

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:34.380
will have their voices heard in court.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.610
There is now nowhere left
for you to hide Larry.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:41.210
More than 160 women say Larry
Nassar sexually abused them.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.470
Before the Center for SafeSport opened

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:46.180
there really wasn't an
organization in this country,

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:49.510
in this world, that focused
on the issues that we do.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:51.530
Within the Olympic and
Paralympic Movement,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.220
national governing bodies
were really responsible

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.680
for investigating any sort of allegation

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.030
that may have come their way,

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:01.010
which some may handled
well, some they didn't.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.920
And what we saw was that

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.960
there was just a conflict
of interest to have

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.640
an organization start to
investigate allegations of abuse

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.180
within their own ranks.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.980
The center did a study last
year where we looked at

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:18.920
data coming from 4,000 athletes
across the Olympic Movement.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.780
And we got representation from every sport

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:24.700
within the Olympic and
Paralympic, which was significant.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.530
And what we found was that

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:30.850
93% of athletes who had experienced abuse

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.200
had not reported it.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.230
That is a significant
number and very troubling.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:38.400
As a movement and as a
community and as an organization

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.690
we have to do more to really help people

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:43.560
understand what abuse looks like

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.500
but also to help them
become more comfortable

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.820
in reporting it.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:48.760
That is the only way

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.023
that we're going to start
shifting the narrative.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:07.060
It's hard to understand until
you're put in that situation

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.590
but he was the person who
was fully developing me

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.490
into who I was becoming.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:15.340
And that is kind of the
power imbalance of it all.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:19.123
And so I just blindly trusted him.

00:09:20.992 --> 00:09:24.370
And I do have to say in
the beginning, I did say no

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.730
I was very firm and I
tried to be supportive

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.320
because I did care about him.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.760
I did have strong relationship with him,

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.230
but I did say no several times.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:37.280
And I was like, that's not
the way I feel about you.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.270
And then he kind of kept pushing

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.623
and I kind of just accepted that.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:47.260
And then that slowly progressed into like

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:48.760
me being at the barn with him.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.720
And he'd pull me aside
on a horse and be like

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:53.460
I just had to tell you
that I'm in love with you.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:56.020
And he was like, I never understood

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:58.393
how I could feel love like this until now.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:03.073
And he'd say stuff like
this is too good to lose.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:07.630
That's probably when I'd say

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.150
that I started to actually love him.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:12.483
I think it lasted around six months.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:18.100
It was just after her 17th birthday

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.650
that their relationship turned sexual.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:24.840
And in the State of Oregon,
the age of consent is 18.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:29.440
Maggie and Rich's relationship
actually ended quite publicly

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.540
at a horse show in Michigan.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.940
She had traveled there with
him and his wife and his son

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:38.500
and they were all sharing an
Airbnb near the show grounds.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.490
And one night his wife,

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.853
Shelley Fellers walked
in on them together.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.180
A lot of the blame was put on me,

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:50.660
even though I didn't really know

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.610
what I'd really gotten myself into.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:56.053
I was kind of just following
the leader who was Rich.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.520
I called my mom, she came to Michigan.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.950
She brought me to a hotel

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:03.560
and I remember just looking
out the hotel window

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.010
looking at the concrete below me thinking

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.090
I understand why people
kill themselves now.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:13.090
Like it was felt like
the only release of pain.

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:14.863
And I was in so much pain.

00:11:17.802 --> 00:11:22.802
And I felt like I had
just lost everything.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:26.420
I had lost the person who I had loved,

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:28.340
the family who I loved.

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:33.340
I had lost my trainers,
my whole support system.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.113
Just everything crashed down real quick.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.800
It was so bad.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:46.100
I think for months and
months, I just operated

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:50.050
as I just have to keep Maggie alive

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.600
and I have to keep my
younger daughter functioning.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.040
That's all I could do.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.913
And I couldn't look up from any of it.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:02.650
In the aftermath of all this

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.180
Maggie wasn't allowed
to return to the stable.

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:09.010
So her and her four
horses never came back.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:11.610
That raised a lot of questions.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:13.670
And on top of that, she's a teenager.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.140
She uses social media

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:18.190
and she was posting
videos of herself crying,

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:20.190
photographs of her with Rich,

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:23.333
song lyrics talking about
how she was in love with him.

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:28.410
More than a dozen people
reported the relationship

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.470
between Rich Fellers and Maggie Kehring

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.940
to the United States Center for SafeSport

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.410
but SafeSport couldn't take any action

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.720
without Maggie's consent.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:41.630
So she decided six months after
the relationship had ended

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:45.280
when she'd gone through
depression, suicidality,

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:49.510
trying to get back on a horse
again, trying to ride again

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.600
trying to find herself again

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.240
that she was going to report him

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.533
to the United States Center for SafeSport.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:59.770
And when she did the
center acted immediately.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:01.700
Police arrested Richard Fellers

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:02.950
a prominent competitor

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:05.060
and trainer in the equestrian industry.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:06.520
And it was the organization,

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:08.620
the U.S. Center for SafeSport

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:11.358
that provided the information to police.

00:13:11.358 --> 00:13:13.860
This here is the 61
year old's booking photo

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:16.200
taken on Monday after
police arrested Fellers

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:19.240
on four counts of second
degree sexual abuse

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:22.600
Rich Fellers was issued a
lifetime ban from SafeSport.

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:24.800
He didn't pursue arbitration

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:28.240
but he has pleaded not guilty
to the charges in court.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.870
A trial date is expected
to be set in April

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.030
and he declined to comment for the story.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.100
A lot of people stood by Rich

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.200
when the initial allegations came out.

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.120
A lot of people attacked Maggie

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.170
and what we've seen in the aftermath

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.560
is this growing sense of people realizing

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:46.530
that actually this is
a problem in the sport.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:49.300
The grooming of young
riders by their coaches

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.130
in powerful positions has happened

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.093
and is still happening today.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:02.150
Up to the end of 2021 SafeSport
had issued 47 sanctions

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.970
against the equestrian community.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:06.730
And this is quite a lot when
you compare it to tennis

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:09.960
an organization that has
eight times as many members

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:13.540
but has had only 35 sanctions
up until that point.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.233
You say the SafeSport needs a lot of work.

00:14:16.233 --> 00:14:20.260
Is this not enough? Is it
not a strong enough system

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:23.700
to protect younger gymnasts
in place right now?

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:26.320
SafeSport's been around
for about five years

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:29.890
and the center has seen its
fair share of criticism.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.490
We have seen gymnasts like Aly Raisman

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:36.110
testifying before Congress saying that

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:39.020
SafeSport doesn't do enough
to support survivors.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:42.420
They try to avoid doing it.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.470
Like they'll say you need to
pass it on to this person.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:46.870
And then the person that we
actually report to will say,

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:48.400
well, actually go back to SafeSport.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.360
It's like they play hot potato

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.440
with who should take the report.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.730
We've seen sports calling out SafeSport

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:58.040
for taking too long in
its investigative process

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.770
for asking too much of survivors

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:03.720
demanding that they
deliver too much evidence

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.510
to prove an allegation.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.250
We pride ourselves on being very thorough.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:10.570
Some investigations
might take a few weeks.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.250
Some may take a few months.

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:14.270
Others have been known to take years

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:17.060
just because of the complexity
of the investigation.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.210
This is not something that we take lightly

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:23.740
because this has so much
impact on people's lives.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:25.530
It is not something that

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:28.773
we are willing to kind of cut corners on.

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:31.850
Equestrian is the on only sport

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:34.790
that is mobilizing against SafeSport

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:37.010
in defense of the accused.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:38.940
We have seen members of this community

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:41.390
create anti SafeSport petitions

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:44.180
that have garnered
thousands of signatures.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:47.250
We've seen it create
nonprofit organizations

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:50.170
which have raised over $2.5 million

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.840
to lobby Congress and challenge
SafeSport's authority,

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.833
to try and limit the powers
that the watchdog has.

00:15:58.300 --> 00:15:59.970
Within the equestrian community

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:02.467
the main criticisms against SafeSport

00:16:02.467 --> 00:16:06.800
are that it lacks due process,
that it lacks transparency

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.620
and that it is effectively
labeling coaches guilty

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:11.253
until proven innocent.

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:20.150
The question about the
extent of the division

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:21.830
within the sport is a good one.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:26.400
My sense from my conversations
with colleague, peers

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:31.533
is that it runs pretty deep.

00:16:35.977 --> 00:16:38.200
In 1989 Ray Texel won

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:42.390
the two most prestigious
medal finals in the U.S.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.110
He's a well-known trainer.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:46.440
He's at the top level of his sport.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.600
And he also feels

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:51.650
as though SafeSport has been
operating like a secret court.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.020
The feeling of it is, you
don't know what's going on

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:58.330
this is not falling in the
criminal justice system

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.880
or the justice system.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.450
It's a step towards it.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.610
And I think that's where a
lot of the division comes from

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:08.300
is not wanting to support
something of that nature.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.660
That's operating in that way.

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:11.510
But at the same time

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:15.530
supporting its message and its purpose.

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:17.510
And there's a conflict there.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:21.470
People in my community are
afraid of, related to SafeSport,

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.570
is very specifically the use

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:29.570
of SafeSport as a weapon,
whether that's for retribution,

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:32.093
whether that's displeasure with somebody,

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:36.333
of course that's a very scary proposition.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.530
So my early thoughts of
SafeSport were definitely

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:46.690
influenced by people around me.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:49.200
And a lot of people were trainers.

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.540
I heard things like
SafeSport is witch hunt.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:53.750
These are innocent trainers,
not doing anything.

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.610
And if clients don't like them

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:59.920
they can go after them
for absolutely anything.

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:02.370
I never really understood
what SafeSport was

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.040
until I actually needed
to go through with it.

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:07.400
And it's a lot different
from what people think

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:09.410
I kind of was like

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.310
I'm just gonna make a social media post.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:14.190
It's going be over,
going to keep moving on.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.910
And then so many women
started reaching out to me,

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.070
so many women and men,

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:21.320
of all ages talking about their stories.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:23.920
And I was like, okay, wait,
I am not the only one.

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:26.540
This is a huge problem in our industry

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.233
that is not talked about enough.

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:31.730
All that's talked about is
how SafeSport is witch hunt

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:35.330
and how SafeSport is awful and
how we need to get rid of it

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:38.420
and how could this be put in place?

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:40.220
And I think a lot of times

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:43.020
some people forget that I'm
still like an 18 year old girl.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.720
Who's coming out the situation.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:48.130
That's not like it's 10 years behind me.

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:49.463
It's still fairly close.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.100
One of the things

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:56.720
that the equestrian
community has struggled with

00:18:56.720 --> 00:19:00.630
is that it's seen some of the
most prestigious trainers,

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:05.630
athletes and Olympic champions
brought down by SafeSport.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:07.610
One thing I've definitely come to realize

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:09.990
over the course of this reporting is that

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:13.093
this is a sport that doesn't
like to watch its heroes fall.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:17.890
For me SafeSport became
the most polarizing

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:22.730
when the person, I think in our community,

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:25.660
that we all looked to the most,

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:29.280
the one with the biggest
voice George Morris,

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.762
my former mentor and trainer.

00:19:31.762 --> 00:19:35.640
When he was set down, I
think that was really maybe

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:37.880
one of the more significant moments

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:41.460
when it really hit hard for many people

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:43.543
that this was real and serious.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:47.500
When George Morris was removed from sport.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.240
I don't think that anyone
inside of SafeSport

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:54.350
could have predicted the just emotional

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:57.770
like outcry of that decision.

00:19:57.770 --> 00:20:00.284
It was something that we
had never seen before.

00:20:00.284 --> 00:20:03.770
The 'I Stand with George'
hashtag was, was circulating.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:07.130
And people were just really
just angry with the center

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:08.680
because this was someone

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:11.360
who had been in this
community for decades.

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:12.820
He was still coaching.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:15.310
He was a pillar within this community.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.690
This guy had his own action figures.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:20.120
Like this was someone that
they really looked up to.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:22.930
And so for him to be called out like this

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:26.543
for him to be removed,
people were just angry.

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:30.800
Within 48 hours of the George Morris ban

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:33.040
a group called 'I Stand With George'

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.660
had popped up on Facebook

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:37.870
and it had more than 4,200 members.

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:40.340
They sent angry emails to SafeSport.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.860
They called the center.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:46.230
They did everything they could
to demand his reinstatement.

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:49.330
They didn't believe that George Morris

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.460
should be brought down by allegations

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.100
dating back to the 1970s.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:58.680
They want to know why and how
SafeSport can operate outside

00:20:58.680 --> 00:21:01.500
and beyond the scope of the
criminal justice system.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:03.840
Not having a statute
of limitations in place

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.780
allowed people to one, take their time

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:10.140
to come to the Center for
SafeSport when they felt ready

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:11.820
but also know that

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:16.380
we were not going to put
some arbitrary timeline

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:19.355
on when you could do that.

00:21:19.355 --> 00:21:22.410
And while this was novel,

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:26.520
I think back in 2017 when we
opened up the organization.

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:28.600
States across this country

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:32.130
are starting to reverse
these statute limitations

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:33.350
on child sexual abuse.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:36.310
And so it is going to become the norm.

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:38.860
George Morris was accused
of sexual misconduct

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:42.480
against two minors
dating back to the 1970s.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.490
In the wake of his lifetime ban

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:46.880
he sought arbitration and lost.

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.765
He's also fighting a civil case

00:21:48.765 --> 00:21:51.690
in the courts against his accuser.

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:53.960
George Morris's lawyer has told us

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:56.413
that he denies any improper conduct.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:21:59.650
You'll see is the higher

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:01.820
that people kind of rise up in their sport

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:04.570
or the better they get or
the more well known they get.

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:05.980
I think there's just more at stake

00:22:05.980 --> 00:22:07.260
and when there's more at stake

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:09.620
people's behavior starts to change.

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:12.350
And so for us really taking to account

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:13.920
the competitiveness of the sport

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:17.090
but also reminding people constantly

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:19.870
that it's not all about
winning at the end of the day

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:21.970
we've gotta make sure
that athletes are safe.

00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:24.040
And that may mean that
we don't win sometimes.

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:24.873
And that's okay.

00:22:26.350 --> 00:22:29.750
Our community for sure stands behind

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:31.520
the rights for victims.

00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:34.144
We want the best for our young

00:22:34.144 --> 00:22:36.390
and we want the best for our old.

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:38.660
So it's not an attack on SafeSport.

00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:43.660
It's not an attack on
anybody, but it's a dialogue.

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:46.200
Is this the best application?

00:23:01.376 --> 00:23:02.209
Your are so beautiful.

00:23:02.209 --> 00:23:05.620
I think that as a reporter,
I'm really grateful

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:10.080
to those who were willing
to open up their lives to us

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:13.200
to sit down and talk
to us to explain about

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:14.730
what had happened to them,

00:23:14.730 --> 00:23:17.373
not just the abuse but what led up to it.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:21.960
One of the things that
Maggie Kehring has done

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:26.100
for this sport is she's
allowed other young people

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:29.673
to step out of the shadows
to break their own silence.

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:37.093
He took away my sense of self, who I was,

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:44.970
my character was very
much built around him

00:23:45.005 --> 00:23:47.233
and everything he had taught me.

00:23:48.690 --> 00:23:51.003
So he shattered who I was as a person.

00:23:52.090 --> 00:23:54.390
Like after that, I felt lost.

00:23:54.390 --> 00:23:56.250
I didn't know who I was anymore.

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:59.550
And even now I'm still
trying to find myself again

00:23:59.550 --> 00:24:03.627
who I am as an individual,
not in that family,

00:24:03.627 --> 00:24:07.923
with those people around
me, influencing who I am.

